  biomeName: Tier 24 East Reserve
  minDepthMeters: 10850
  maxDepthMeters: 11375
  shortDescription: Reserved biome slot for Tier 24 / East. The 108-biome matrix
    expects a bespoke authored identity here; final lore and geology are pending
    expansion from the master vision.
  isPlaceholder: 1
  visitPurpose: Late-game pressure biome. Come here only for major progress, rare
    extraction, and to read walls, fissures, and major vertical routes.
  commonRewardHook: Even routine value here comes from Abyssal Crystal and Rare Earth
    Dust.
  rareRewardHook: 'The reason to risk the trip is: Gold Ore and Abyss Pressure Shell.'
  landmarkIdentity: Tier 24 East Reserve reads through walls, fins, fissures, and
    giant vertical breaks. Landmarks should feel singular and intimidating.
  safePocketIdentity: Safe pockets are almost psychological only. The player survives
    by discipline, not comfort.
  riskSummary: 'Main failure mode: vertical trap geometry and hard commitment, depth
    stress, and expensive hesitation. Creature pressure stays extreme.'
  extractionFocus: 'Minimal contact count, extreme commitment, almost no comfort.
    Deep tier: work edges, cracks, and vertical seams, extract only what justifies
    the risk, and leave cleanly.'
  landmarkGuidance: Dominant landmark is the final shaft or void cut. This slot should
    read through a singular abyssal absence in the world; use walls and breaks to
    mark route commitment.
